1
00:00:00,373 --> 00:00:06,356
(A Bona fide Killer)

2
00:00:08,349 --> 00:00:10,172
(This drama, its characters,
and events are fictional.)

3
00:00:10,196 --> 00:00:11,345
(Scenes with child actors
and animals were supervised.)

4
00:00:11,643 --> 00:00:13,879
(2018 South Korea VS Germany)

5
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:19,041
- Korea.
- Korea.

6
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:22,211
- Korea.
- Korea.

7
00:00:24,613 --> 00:00:25,614
(Episode 7)

8
00:00:25,614 --> 00:00:27,083
Pickpockets are running wild
in the square,

9
00:00:27,083 --> 00:00:28,517
taking advantage of the World Cup crowds.

10
00:00:30,319 --> 00:00:31,687
Pickpockets. Pickpockets.

11
00:00:34,824 --> 00:00:38,194
I love soccer, but I'm telling you,
I'm not here for fun.

12
00:00:38,227 --> 00:00:41,063
Who knows? They might even put out
a composite sketch of me.

13
00:00:45,601 --> 00:00:48,604
And I've prepared the perfect bait.

14
00:00:52,408 --> 00:00:53,709
I'm hanging up.

15
00:00:53,743 --> 00:00:56,345
Hey. You in the red hat. Stop.

16
00:01:00,015 --> 00:01:01,016
That one's a fake.

17
00:01:03,085 --> 00:01:04,854
This is the real one, full of cash.

18
00:01:06,088 --> 00:01:07,256
Darn it...

19
00:01:13,262 --> 00:01:14,263
If you don't want your picture taken,

20
00:01:15,097 --> 00:01:16,098
let's at least do an interview.

21
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:20,669
The old man says to lie low for a while.

22
00:01:21,570 --> 00:01:23,906
And you know I always listen
to our money man.

23
00:01:23,906 --> 00:01:25,841
But I heard
that delivery schmuck who died

24
00:01:25,841 --> 00:01:26,942
was a widower with two kids.

25
00:01:27,877 --> 00:01:30,646
Dude, of all the people
to hit with your car...

26
00:01:31,046 --> 00:01:33,182
What the hell are you talking about?

27
00:01:33,182 --> 00:01:36,051
The front of my quarter-million-dollar car
is totaled.

28
00:01:36,819 --> 00:01:38,954
I'm the victim here.

29
00:01:38,954 --> 00:01:40,723
Hey, hey, we scored a goal.

30
00:01:40,723 --> 00:01:43,659
- Hey, they scored.
- So what?

31
00:01:43,659 --> 00:01:44,960
Hello?

32
00:01:49,365 --> 00:01:53,035
I'm so damn annoyed right now,
and these pathetic losers...

33
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:57,840
Korea's a damn honey pot, you bastards.

34
00:02:28,971 --> 00:02:29,972
Meeting's over.

35
00:02:32,308 --> 00:02:33,342
Is it over?

36
00:02:35,911 --> 00:02:36,946
It's finally over.

37
00:02:37,747 --> 00:02:40,649
Relax, rookie.
And stretch out that cramp in your leg.

38
00:02:41,317 --> 00:02:43,652
What? Nervous? I wasn't...

39
00:02:50,025 --> 00:02:51,727
Half of any Meeting is just waiting.

40
00:02:53,362 --> 00:02:54,563
And what else do you need?

41
00:02:54,997 --> 00:02:55,998
Endurance.

42
00:02:57,099 --> 00:02:58,567
I guess I need to do
some strength training.

43
00:02:59,568 --> 00:03:00,736
Nice work.

44
00:03:03,406 --> 00:03:05,074
You're pretty skilled too, rookie.

45
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:07,910
I can leave things in your hands.

46
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:08,911
What?

47
00:03:09,445 --> 00:03:11,947
Leave? Where? Who's leaving?

48
00:03:11,947 --> 00:03:14,083
That was excellent for a first Meeting.
Good job.

49
00:03:17,253 --> 00:03:18,821
Take the emergency stairs
to the first floor.

50
00:03:19,488 --> 00:03:21,690
Go out through Gate Three
and blend into the crowd.

51
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:23,626
Okay.

52
00:03:28,064 --> 00:03:30,099
But what about you?
It's too bad you're missing the game.

53
00:03:30,099 --> 00:03:31,167
I'm not interested.

54
00:03:31,634 --> 00:03:32,902
Really? That's unusual.

55
00:03:33,702 --> 00:03:35,071
You're not interested either, are you?

56
00:03:35,638 --> 00:03:37,973
That must be why you scheduled
the Meeting for today.

57
00:03:37,973 --> 00:03:40,709
Hey, that's because a day like today
is advantageous for a Meeting.

58
00:03:42,945 --> 00:03:45,347
But besides work,

59
00:03:46,048 --> 00:03:48,417
do you have any other interests?

60
00:03:56,292 --> 00:04:00,262
Are you picking up any movement right now?
Near the emergency stairs?

61
00:04:00,262 --> 00:04:01,263
What?

62
00:04:05,835 --> 00:04:09,271
No. Besides the security office,
the entire building is empty.

63
00:04:09,905 --> 00:04:12,274
Then rewind and check
if we missed anything.

64
00:04:12,274 --> 00:04:13,642
From after I came up.

65
00:04:13,642 --> 00:04:14,710
Is something wrong?

66
00:04:14,744 --> 00:04:16,178
Report back if you find anything.

67
00:04:45,808 --> 00:04:48,277
(Resident Id Card: Kwon Tae Sung)

68
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:56,685
(Reporter, Not Today, Kwon Tae Sung)

69
00:05:04,326 --> 00:05:06,262
(Gate 3)

70
00:05:08,264 --> 00:05:09,665
(Emergency Stairs Exit)

71
00:05:09,665 --> 00:05:10,933
Hey.

72
00:05:10,966 --> 00:05:13,769
About 10 minutes ago,
2 men ran in through Gate 3.

73
00:05:14,470 --> 00:05:16,105
It looked like one was chasing the other.

74
00:05:17,006 --> 00:05:18,441
They entered the emergency stairs
one after the other,

75
00:05:19,642 --> 00:05:22,478
and five minutes later,
only the one who went in first came out.

76
00:05:24,346 --> 00:05:25,414
I missed it.

77
00:05:26,215 --> 00:05:29,452
- I'm sorry.
- Okay. Keep your eyes on it.

78
00:05:29,485 --> 00:05:31,654
But what's...

79
00:05:35,424 --> 00:05:36,692
You should have been more careful.

80
00:05:42,665 --> 00:05:44,300
(Connecting to Emergency Services: 911)

81
00:05:46,435 --> 00:05:47,737
Yes, this is the Kingtower Building.

82
00:05:47,737 --> 00:05:49,371
On the fifth floor
of the emergency stairwell,

83
00:05:49,371 --> 00:05:51,707
there's a man collapsed
and bleeding from his head.

84
00:05:51,707 --> 00:05:53,175
I think he'll die if you don't hurry.

85
00:06:09,358 --> 00:06:10,726
Try to live, if you can.

86
00:06:10,726 --> 00:06:12,027
It looks like we won the soccer game.

87
00:06:13,329 --> 00:06:14,897
Because one is enough for today.

88
00:06:22,071 --> 00:06:24,340
(4 Months Later)

89
00:06:24,673 --> 00:06:27,743
- Hold still. Stay still.
- Why? Goodness.

90
00:06:27,777 --> 00:06:30,813
- Let me see for a second.
- What? Seriously, what's wrong?

91
00:06:35,217 --> 00:06:36,352
Your head's still attached.

92
00:06:36,919 --> 00:06:38,687
You're insane, aren't you?

93
00:06:39,722 --> 00:06:42,892
That's right. I can start walking today.

94
00:06:42,892 --> 00:06:45,728
Hey, hey.

95
00:06:47,363 --> 00:06:48,397
This feels weird.

96
00:06:48,431 --> 00:06:50,599
If you see a pickpocket,
you're supposed to call the police.

97
00:06:50,599 --> 00:06:53,469
- Why would you chase them, you idiot?
- I think I have a cramp.

98
00:06:55,571 --> 00:06:57,740
How can you lecture me
about the same thing every time you visit?

99
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:01,077
You're unbelievable.
I'm so sick of hearing it.

100
00:07:02,078 --> 00:07:03,746
You think this is funny?
You're laughing right now?

101
00:07:04,046 --> 00:07:06,449
You woke up after four months, you idiot.

102
00:07:06,449 --> 00:07:08,818
Calling a patient with a head injury
an idiot over and over.

103
00:07:12,288 --> 00:07:15,291
Right. You still haven't caught the guy
who hit me from behind.

104
00:07:15,291 --> 00:07:18,461
- Don't you dare go trying to catch him.
- Why?

105
00:07:19,228 --> 00:07:20,796
You look like you'd actually kill him
if you caught him.

106
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,765
Of course I'd kill him.
That bastard. You...

107
00:07:29,038 --> 00:07:30,639
The rooftop of the building
where you collapsed,

108
00:07:30,673 --> 00:07:32,641
did you know that was
Kingfisher's sniping point?

109
00:07:33,075 --> 00:07:35,778
I know. It's such a shame, seriously.

110
00:07:35,778 --> 00:07:37,446
If I hadn't been hit
in the back of the head,

111
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:40,850
- I could have met Kingfisher.
- You could have met them, I guess.

112
00:07:40,850 --> 00:07:43,619
But you'd have a hole
in your head instead, you idiot.

113
00:07:43,619 --> 00:07:46,489
Hey, that's slander against Kingfisher.

114
00:07:46,489 --> 00:07:48,924
Why? Because I'm an innocent civilian.

115
00:07:51,193 --> 00:07:53,496
I can't tell if this guy is lucky
or unlucky.

116
00:07:54,597 --> 00:07:57,633
I really worry about the kind of woman
who'll end up with you.

117
00:08:00,136 --> 00:08:01,504
(Ward 22)

118
00:08:21,457 --> 00:08:24,093
Manager Yu, you visit so often.
You're making me feel bad.

119
00:08:24,126 --> 00:08:26,295
It's not like being sick is a big deal.

120
00:08:26,328 --> 00:08:27,963
You were injured on the job.

121
00:08:29,632 --> 00:08:30,966
How are you feeling?

122
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,370
Maybe it's my age,
but this isn't healing well.

123
00:08:34,904 --> 00:08:37,373
I know. Everyone's going through a lot
because of me.

124
00:08:37,406 --> 00:08:39,108
Everyone is very worried.

125
00:08:39,508 --> 00:08:40,509
You know you need to be careful...

126
00:08:40,543 --> 00:08:42,311
about aftereffects
from the car accident, right?

127
00:08:42,344 --> 00:08:43,612
Well, this...

128
00:08:45,214 --> 00:08:46,749
Darn...

129
00:08:46,782 --> 00:08:47,783
This is good.

130
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,155
Oh man, this...

131
00:08:54,490 --> 00:08:55,891
- This?
- Yes.

132
00:09:03,332 --> 00:09:04,333
By the way,

133
00:09:05,067 --> 00:09:06,736
I hear the new recruit
is pretty competent.

134
00:09:07,770 --> 00:09:09,505
Yes, after Assistant Manager Son quit,

135
00:09:09,972 --> 00:09:12,742
I was worried his absence
would leave a big hole.

136
00:09:12,742 --> 00:09:15,077
But now I can breathe a sigh of relief.

137
00:09:16,045 --> 00:09:19,515
Your absence is felt even more, sir.
Please get well soon and come back.

138
00:09:19,949 --> 00:09:22,752
I can't leave with peace of mind
until you're back.

139
00:09:25,454 --> 00:09:27,690
Manager Yu, have you made up your mind?

140
00:09:28,591 --> 00:09:30,860
Are you really going to quit?

141
00:09:32,061 --> 00:09:33,362
I think I'm just worn out.

142
00:09:34,330 --> 00:09:35,598
Yes, that's understandable.

143
00:09:36,132 --> 00:09:39,468
Even ordinary people,
after working for ten years,

144
00:09:39,468 --> 00:09:42,438
they say they experience
that thing, burnout.

145
00:09:42,471 --> 00:09:44,774
You've done nothing but work
without a break,

146
00:09:44,774 --> 00:09:46,075
so it's no wonder you're exhausted.

147
00:09:47,376 --> 00:09:48,444
Right?

148
00:09:50,546 --> 00:09:52,848
Besides, your line of work
isn't exactly ordinary, is it?

149
00:09:53,682 --> 00:09:56,552
It's a thankless job that never ends.

150
00:09:57,319 --> 00:09:59,321
And the world never changes.

151
00:10:00,256 --> 00:10:03,526
I completely understand how you feel.

152
00:10:04,493 --> 00:10:05,528
Manager Yu.

153
00:10:07,062 --> 00:10:08,964
Won't you please reconsider?

154
00:10:09,398 --> 00:10:12,334
Don't go to the field Meetings
for a while.

155
00:10:12,768 --> 00:10:14,103
Just take it easy.

156
00:10:15,337 --> 00:10:16,439
Okay?

157
00:10:57,012 --> 00:10:59,048
Just a moment. Just...

158
00:11:02,318 --> 00:11:03,352
Get down. Come down, quickly.

159
00:11:08,991 --> 00:11:10,793
Okay, easy now. Be careful.

160
00:11:12,728 --> 00:11:13,729
Why?

161
00:11:14,997 --> 00:11:15,998
What?

162
00:11:16,465 --> 00:11:17,800
Why? Why?

163
00:11:18,501 --> 00:11:19,502
Why?

164
00:11:21,504 --> 00:11:22,738
Because life is precious.

165
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:25,775
What I mean is...

166
00:11:26,809 --> 00:11:30,713
I recently had a near-death experience,
and it made me realize something. So...

167
00:11:31,547 --> 00:11:34,717
You know, you look at the sky,
you look at the autumn leaves.

168
00:11:35,551 --> 00:11:36,852
I'm glad to be alive.

169
00:11:38,554 --> 00:11:39,889
It's so good to be alive.

170
00:11:40,723 --> 00:11:45,728
You get to joke around with your friends,
get nagged by your family.

171
00:11:45,761 --> 00:11:47,363
What should I eat today?
What should I wear tomorrow?

172
00:11:47,363 --> 00:11:50,866
An ordinary life where you worry
about such trivial things...

173
00:11:50,866 --> 00:11:53,736
is so precious. Truly precious.

174
00:11:54,270 --> 00:11:55,271
That's why I...

175
00:11:58,641 --> 00:12:00,976
hope that you will choose to live.

176
00:12:39,448 --> 00:12:41,117
Someone who says life is precious
is smoking a cigarette?

177
00:12:41,851 --> 00:12:44,520
Especially after a near-death experience.
Doesn't that seem wrong to you?

178
00:12:44,553 --> 00:12:46,689
This isn't mine. I was just on my way...

179
00:12:50,493 --> 00:12:53,829
Live a good life.
Enjoy your ordinary, day-to-day life.

180
00:12:55,564 --> 00:12:56,632
Excuse me.

181
00:12:59,735 --> 00:13:01,404
Have we met before?

182
00:13:05,574 --> 00:13:06,876
No.

183
00:13:06,876 --> 00:13:08,177
But I'm sure I've seen you before...

184
00:13:08,978 --> 00:13:10,079
Your voice sounds familiar too.

185
00:13:13,582 --> 00:13:14,650
I'm sorry. I...

186
00:13:15,551 --> 00:13:18,220
I hurt my head,
so I think my mind's a little fuzzy.

187
00:13:19,455 --> 00:13:22,391
I guess my memory will come back
once I recover. Right?

188
00:13:24,827 --> 00:13:27,730
Kwon Tae Sung.
He's a reporter for an online news outlet.

189
00:13:27,763 --> 00:13:30,366
I looked through some of
his past articles,

190
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,335
and his main interests are social justice
and protecting the weak.

191
00:13:33,369 --> 00:13:36,372
He's a rare breed of reporter these days.
But why him?

192
00:13:37,673 --> 00:13:41,510
- Just a precaution. Keep going.
- Is it because of this?

193
00:13:41,544 --> 00:13:42,645
(Kingfisher)

194
00:13:42,678 --> 00:13:45,714
It seems he's written all of
this outlet's articles on Kingfisher.

195
00:13:46,515 --> 00:13:48,751
I skimmed through them,

196
00:13:48,784 --> 00:13:51,220
and he didn't really have a negative take
on Kingfisher.

197
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:53,756
It was more about analyzing the phenomenon
than following the incidents.

198
00:13:53,756 --> 00:13:55,524
So among others in the industry
and readers,

199
00:13:55,524 --> 00:13:57,726
they seem to be well-regarded
as in-depth articles.

200
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,930
And he also has a personal blog.

201
00:14:01,897 --> 00:14:03,899
Send me the link.
And the articles. Right now.

202
00:14:04,533 --> 00:14:05,534
All of them?

203
00:14:08,104 --> 00:14:11,073
I mean, she usually couldn't care less
about articles...

204
00:14:18,681 --> 00:14:21,784
<i>Kingfisher, Unprecedented</i>
<i>Murderer or Arbiter of Justice?</i>

205
00:14:21,784 --> 00:14:23,385
<i>The Painful Questions Kingfisher Raises</i>
<i>for Our Society.</i>

206
00:14:23,385 --> 00:14:25,187
<i>Five Reflections on Kingfisher.</i>

207
00:14:25,187 --> 00:14:27,223
<i>Is Our Judicial System</i>
<i>Sufficiently Trustworthy?</i>

208
00:14:27,957 --> 00:14:29,558
<i>If I Were to Meet Kingfisher.</i>

209
00:14:30,793 --> 00:14:34,663
<i>Fortunately, I had a smooth upbringing</i>
<i>in a happy home,</i>

210
00:14:34,697 --> 00:14:35,731
<i>and throughout my school years,</i>

211
00:14:35,731 --> 00:14:38,367
<i>I was an ordinary, model student</i>
<i>for the most part.</i>

212
00:14:38,367 --> 00:14:39,402
Best two out of three?
Loser buys pizza.

213
00:14:40,536 --> 00:14:42,271
Don't be a sore loser, or you're dead.

214
00:14:42,972 --> 00:14:44,974
You're the one who shouldn't be crying
when you lose, you jerk.

215
00:14:44,974 --> 00:14:47,643
- Hey, how many times have you lost?
- Whatever.

216
00:15:07,129 --> 00:15:09,198
<i>If it weren't</i>
<i>for the tragic incident</i>

217
00:15:09,198 --> 00:15:10,499
<i>that befell a friend of mine,</i>

218
00:15:10,499 --> 00:15:13,102
<i>I might have lived my whole life</i>
<i>far removed...</i>

219
00:15:13,102 --> 00:15:14,804
<i>from things like crime and illegal acts.</i>

220
00:15:14,804 --> 00:15:17,306
A murder involving
a sniper rifle has occurred...

221
00:15:17,339 --> 00:15:19,308
in the heart of downtown Seoul.

222
00:15:19,308 --> 00:15:20,776
- According to police, Semyeong-dong...
- A gun?

223
00:15:20,810 --> 00:15:23,712
- A man in his 40s was shot...
- What are they going to do?

224
00:15:23,712 --> 00:15:26,849
<i>I still remember the shock</i>
<i>of when I first learned of his existence.</i>

225
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:30,419
<i>To think there was someone</i>
<i>who only targeted vicious criminals,</i>

226
00:15:30,419 --> 00:15:33,522
<i>the kind who destroy the lives</i>
<i>of ordinary, innocent people.</i>

227
00:15:33,522 --> 00:15:35,925
Honestly, isn't Kingfisher kind of cool?

228
00:15:35,925 --> 00:15:38,727
What's cool about him?
He's just a crazy murderer.

229
00:15:38,727 --> 00:15:41,130
Hey, but he only kills bad guys.

230
00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:45,735
Hey, even if he only kills
bad guys, a murderer is still a murderer.

231
00:15:46,569 --> 00:15:49,038
<i>While the world was loudly</i>
<i>debating and taking sides,</i>

232
00:15:49,038 --> 00:15:50,439
<i>I found myself wondering.</i>

233
00:15:51,507 --> 00:15:54,543
<i>What kind of person would risk</i>
<i>their entire life...</i>

234
00:15:54,543 --> 00:15:55,711
<i>to do something like that?</i>

235
00:16:03,486 --> 00:16:05,054
(Reporter Attacked By Pickpockets
Wakes After Four Months)

236
00:16:05,054 --> 00:16:07,757
At the time of the incident, Reporter Kwon
was in a building in downtown Seoul...

237
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:10,459
(Rooftop Where Reporter Kwon Collapsed
Was Kingfisher's Sniping Position)

238
00:16:39,989 --> 00:16:43,159
Have we met before?
Once I've fully recovered,

239
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:45,661
my memories will slowly come back, right?

240
00:16:52,034 --> 00:16:54,437
(Gyeongsan Hospital)

241
00:17:04,713 --> 00:17:05,748
(2018 First-Class ICU Rating)

242
00:17:08,984 --> 00:17:11,320
- You didn't make this.
- I did make it.

243
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:13,722
- You bought this.
- No, I made it. Try some.

244
00:17:15,124 --> 00:17:16,859
- How is it?
- Tastes store-bought.

245
00:17:16,859 --> 00:17:17,860
No, it doesn't.

246
00:17:18,427 --> 00:17:21,864
I really, really made this. I'm serious.

247
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,234
How about this one?

248
00:17:26,535 --> 00:17:28,237
- It's good.
- That's it?

249
00:17:29,004 --> 00:17:31,173
What? What else am I supposed
to say? It's...it's good.

250
00:17:31,173 --> 00:17:32,908
I made it, and I think
I did a really good job.

251
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:39,448
Excuse me, miss! Just a moment.

252
00:17:40,916 --> 00:17:42,518
I finally found her.

253
00:17:43,519 --> 00:17:45,688
I've been waiting for you. Every day.

254
00:17:46,088 --> 00:17:47,089
Why?

255
00:17:47,723 --> 00:17:49,658
Because I remembered where we met.

256
00:17:52,795 --> 00:17:54,163
You lived in Hoehun-dong as a kid, right?

257
00:17:56,665 --> 00:17:57,767
No, I've never lived there.

258
00:18:00,803 --> 00:18:02,838
You went to Jeongin Middle School,
didn't you? I'm right, aren't I?

259
00:18:02,838 --> 00:18:04,006
No.

260
00:18:07,009 --> 00:18:09,245
- The Hwaljjak Binnari Academy...
- No.

261
00:18:13,516 --> 00:18:15,518
Has anyone told you
you look like the actress Choi So Hyun...

262
00:18:16,652 --> 00:18:18,053
No, they haven't. Right.

263
00:18:20,222 --> 00:18:24,560
I'm sorry.
I'll try to jog my memory better,

264
00:18:25,127 --> 00:18:27,797
and I'll be sure
to get it right next time.

265
00:18:36,272 --> 00:18:39,375
You might be misunderstanding this,
thinking I'm hitting on you,

266
00:18:39,375 --> 00:18:40,976
but that's not it at all. Absolutely not.

267
00:18:41,010 --> 00:18:42,912
If we happen to have a chance
to meet again...

268
00:18:42,912 --> 00:18:46,215
No, that's not going to happen.
Don't do anything pointless.

269
00:18:47,416 --> 00:18:48,651
We've never met.

270
00:18:53,422 --> 00:18:54,457
Gosh.

271
00:18:54,490 --> 00:18:55,925
(Gyeongsan Hospital Screening Center)

272
00:18:57,460 --> 00:18:59,328
I should have asked for her name.

273
00:19:08,537 --> 00:19:09,739
<i> Are you having trouble sleeping?</i>

274
00:19:10,239 --> 00:19:13,175
You wake up soon after falling asleep,
and you have nightmares sometimes?

275
00:19:13,943 --> 00:19:15,177
Yes, I guess.

276
00:19:15,211 --> 00:19:17,980
Have you been under
a lot of stress recently?

277
00:19:22,885 --> 00:19:25,087
Maybe some trouble in your relationships,

278
00:19:25,087 --> 00:19:27,022
or feeling pressured at work?

279
00:19:30,459 --> 00:19:33,696
- No, I haven't.
- No, not at all.

280
00:19:34,497 --> 00:19:38,801
I see. I can prescribe you
a higher dose of sleeping pills, but...

281
00:19:39,268 --> 00:19:40,369
in my opinion...

282
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:48,844
Are you having fun?

283
00:19:48,844 --> 00:19:50,146
Mi Ju, how do you like it? Is it okay?

284
00:19:51,647 --> 00:19:52,948
But isn't it really pretty here?

285
00:19:57,186 --> 00:19:59,789
- Really? Good job.
- You want to hold it?

286
00:19:59,789 --> 00:20:00,790
No.

287
00:20:01,857 --> 00:20:04,193
Hey, we won over here. Mom.

288
00:20:09,698 --> 00:20:10,900
(Team Leader Bae Yoon OK, Sales Team 3)

289
00:20:12,768 --> 00:20:13,936
I'm resigning.

290
00:20:14,937 --> 00:20:16,739
Please accept it, Team Leader.

291
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:47,903
- He's coming out.
- There he is. Excuse me.

292
00:20:47,937 --> 00:20:50,339
Do we know how two people
were taken down in the same room?

293
00:20:50,339 --> 00:20:51,507
What if there was only one target,

294
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:53,542
- and Kingfisher made a mistake?
- We're not police officers.

295
00:20:53,576 --> 00:20:55,077
We're just office workers
on our lunch break.

296
00:20:55,077 --> 00:20:56,345
- They said they aren't.
- They're not cops?

297
00:20:56,345 --> 00:20:57,346
What's going on?

298
00:21:01,050 --> 00:21:02,351
You're a good liar.

299
00:21:02,351 --> 00:21:04,253
Well, I was half-telling the truth.

300
00:21:04,286 --> 00:21:06,255
It's true that we're not the cops
in charge of this jurisdiction.

301
00:21:06,288 --> 00:21:08,124
I'm so hungry I could pass out.

302
00:21:08,124 --> 00:21:10,226
All I had last night were
two of those chocolate pies.

303
00:21:10,226 --> 00:21:12,027
I only had one cream bun.

304
00:21:12,061 --> 00:21:13,262
Oh, right.

305
00:21:14,497 --> 00:21:15,731
Goodness.

306
00:21:15,731 --> 00:21:18,467
But I guess "One shot, two kills"
is a hot topic, as expected.

307
00:21:18,501 --> 00:21:20,703
It's the 1st case like it in 16 years.

308
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:23,205
The internet is going crazy over it too,

309
00:21:23,205 --> 00:21:25,040
that the original target
was just Tak Jong Gu,

310
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,042
and that they accidentally killed
an innocent person trying to shoot him.

311
00:21:27,042 --> 00:21:30,112
Do you really think Kingfisher is someone
who would make that kind of mistake?

312
00:21:30,146 --> 00:21:31,414
Oh, no. He's not that type at all.

313
00:21:32,014 --> 00:21:34,283
Anyway, setting Tak Jong Gu aside.

314
00:21:34,283 --> 00:21:37,052
What did that Chairman Cheon
what's-his-name do to deserve it?

315
00:21:37,086 --> 00:21:40,689
That's what we need to find out now.
Why Cheon Seong Gil was a target.

316
00:21:41,891 --> 00:21:43,926
Right now? Without eating first?

317
00:21:44,527 --> 00:21:46,562
Come on, sir,
I've only had two chocolate pies...

318
00:21:46,562 --> 00:21:47,630
Hey, wait up.

319
00:21:47,630 --> 00:21:51,000
This case is unusual
not only because there were two deaths,

320
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,735
but because the criminal history...

321
00:21:52,768 --> 00:21:54,670
of one of the victims
hasn't been identified.

322
00:21:55,271 --> 00:21:58,040
This has led to speculation
that Kingfisher may have mistakenly...

323
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:00,042
killed an innocent person.

324
00:22:00,042 --> 00:22:01,644
If that turns out to be true,

325
00:22:01,644 --> 00:22:03,546
it could cause
a major shift in public opinion, right?

326
00:22:03,546 --> 00:22:05,881
Until now, the belief was
that he only killed vicious criminals...

327
00:22:06,382 --> 00:22:08,617
- Yes, Reporter Koo.
- Hey, where are you?

328
00:22:09,051 --> 00:22:10,886
The informant
on the Cheon Seong Gil case called.

329
00:22:10,886 --> 00:22:11,987
They're willing to do an interview.

330
00:22:12,955 --> 00:22:14,657
I've arranged to meet them right now.

331
00:22:16,292 --> 00:22:17,293
Hello?

332
00:22:18,394 --> 00:22:20,696
Hey? Are you there? Are you listening?

333
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:22,865
Where did you agree to meet?

334
00:22:22,898 --> 00:22:24,700
(Taesung Chicken)

335
00:22:30,005 --> 00:22:32,608
- I'm here, Mother.
- Oh, welcome...

336
00:22:32,942 --> 00:22:34,477
What are you doing here at this hour?

337
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:37,346
- Didn't you go to work?
- No, my business trip ended a day early,

338
00:22:37,446 --> 00:22:38,948
so I don't have to go in today.

339
00:22:39,315 --> 00:22:42,585
And I bought you something, Mother.

340
00:22:42,585 --> 00:22:45,154
Oh? What's this?

341
00:22:45,187 --> 00:22:46,355
(Lipiera)

342
00:22:46,388 --> 00:22:49,191
Since you haven't been sleeping well
at night lately,

343
00:22:49,225 --> 00:22:51,560
and you've been having
hot and cold flashes.

344
00:22:52,161 --> 00:22:55,331
I have been feeling flushed lately, but...

345
00:22:55,698 --> 00:22:58,067
I wonder why that is.

346
00:22:58,601 --> 00:23:01,003
Mother, they say it's all
because of menopause.

347
00:23:01,036 --> 00:23:02,972
But one of these a day
can help you manage...

348
00:23:04,106 --> 00:23:05,574
Really.

349
00:23:06,208 --> 00:23:08,144
Is there anything I can help you with?

350
00:23:08,177 --> 00:23:09,578
Help with what?

351
00:23:09,578 --> 00:23:11,213
You must be tired from your trip.
Go home and get some rest.

352
00:23:11,714 --> 00:23:13,015
No, I'm fine.

353
00:23:13,449 --> 00:23:17,386
It's not like you're trying to mock me.
Hey, if you have eyes, take a look.

354
00:23:17,787 --> 00:23:21,157
Is there anything here to help with?
My goodness.

355
00:23:21,157 --> 00:23:22,892
Even if there was, so what?

356
00:23:22,925 --> 00:23:24,627
Do you think I could
bring myself to ask you?

357
00:23:25,094 --> 00:23:28,097
As if I'd dare to overwork
my precious daughter-in-law.

358
00:23:28,097 --> 00:23:30,866
Then I'd just get an earful
from my son again.

359
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:33,436
Mom, why are you
taking it out on her again?

360
00:23:34,236 --> 00:23:35,438
- No, it's fine.
- Business is slow,

361
00:23:35,471 --> 00:23:36,705
so she's just taking it out on you.

362
00:23:38,808 --> 00:23:42,411
Mother, this also helps with
mood swings from menopause.

363
00:23:43,112 --> 00:23:45,014
So, what should I peel?

364
00:23:45,047 --> 00:23:46,749
What?

365
00:23:47,216 --> 00:23:49,251
- Welcome.
- Hello.

366
00:23:49,251 --> 00:23:51,287
- Welcome. Oh my.
- Hello.

367
00:23:51,287 --> 00:23:53,155
Welcome. Please have a seat here.

368
00:23:53,155 --> 00:23:54,223
Yes, sit right here.

369
00:23:55,091 --> 00:23:56,926
President Kim, what a surprise.

370
00:23:56,959 --> 00:23:59,028
I was just at
the Merchants' Association meeting.

371
00:23:59,028 --> 00:24:02,264
- We came for lunch after it ended.
- Thank you.

372
00:24:02,298 --> 00:24:05,067
About 20 more people will be coming later.

373
00:24:05,067 --> 00:24:06,936
The manager of the senior center
in the next town...

374
00:24:06,936 --> 00:24:09,071
was looking for a good chicken place,

375
00:24:09,105 --> 00:24:12,408
- so I recommended you.
- Oh my goodness.

376
00:24:13,008 --> 00:24:15,811
President Kim, you're a lifesaver.
A true lifesaver.

377
00:24:15,811 --> 00:24:17,980
Just wait a moment.
I'll make it delicious for you.

378
00:24:18,013 --> 00:24:19,115
Order whenever you're ready, okay?

379
00:24:21,617 --> 00:24:23,452
Yes, Taesung Chicken.

380
00:24:24,386 --> 00:24:28,190
Yes, the child welfare center?
Yes, I know it.

381
00:24:28,190 --> 00:24:31,494
Yes. What? Twenty chickens?

382
00:24:31,527 --> 00:24:32,928
By five o'clock?

383
00:24:34,029 --> 00:24:37,466
Yes. We'll make them delicious
and send them over. Okay.

384
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,402
Twenty Chickens?

385
00:24:39,435 --> 00:24:41,270
- Yes.
- What is happening?

386
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:44,507
What do you mean? It's our lucky day.
Quick, fry the chicken, fry the chicken.

387
00:24:44,507 --> 00:24:45,574
Okay.

388
00:24:45,608 --> 00:24:48,010
We're in trouble, the chicken...
Oh my, now we're really in a jam.

389
00:24:51,614 --> 00:24:53,649
Is Yul's mom still here?

390
00:24:55,284 --> 00:24:56,385
Mother, I'm right here.

391
00:24:58,120 --> 00:24:59,221
- Thank you for your time today.
- Of course.

392
00:24:59,221 --> 00:25:00,523
- Thank you.
- Get home safe now.

393
00:25:00,956 --> 00:25:01,957
Take care.

394
00:25:06,128 --> 00:25:08,964
This worked out so well, didn't it?

395
00:25:09,765 --> 00:25:12,835
I was wondering how I'd write the article
without testimony or evidence.

396
00:25:12,868 --> 00:25:15,638
It couldn't have been easy,
but she worked up the courage.

397
00:25:15,638 --> 00:25:18,074
What, an innocent life?

398
00:25:18,974 --> 00:25:21,577
He has no idea how evil a man
Cheon Seong Gil is.

399
00:25:22,044 --> 00:25:24,046
Let's go.

400
00:25:27,516 --> 00:25:30,219
But seriously,
your instincts are incredible.

401
00:25:30,786 --> 00:25:32,988
It was the same with Pyo Gyu Cheol.

402
00:25:32,988 --> 00:25:36,492
How do you manage to pinpoint
Kingfisher's targets like that?

403
00:25:37,293 --> 00:25:38,427
At this rate...

404
00:25:38,427 --> 00:25:41,697
Don't you think we might run into
Kingfisher somewhere?

405
00:25:42,164 --> 00:25:45,568
I wonder if we've already
crossed paths without knowing.

406
00:25:47,069 --> 00:25:48,137
Reporter Koo, aren't you scared?

407
00:25:48,137 --> 00:25:49,839
About what might happen
if you meet Kingfisher?

408
00:25:50,439 --> 00:25:53,442
What? Of what?

409
00:25:53,442 --> 00:25:55,811
I'm an innocent citizen.

410
00:25:56,879 --> 00:25:58,481
Let's go.

411
00:26:01,417 --> 00:26:03,753
- It's hot, so please be careful.
- Ma'am.

412
00:26:03,786 --> 00:26:04,820
- Yes?
- One more fried chicken.

413
00:26:04,820 --> 00:26:06,756
One fried chicken. Hey,
another order of fried chicken.

414
00:26:06,789 --> 00:26:08,190
- Got it.
- Okay.

415
00:26:08,224 --> 00:26:09,725
- Excuse me, one coke, please.
- You want a coke?

416
00:26:09,759 --> 00:26:12,962
I'll get the coke. Here you go.
Take these empty glasses.

417
00:26:12,962 --> 00:26:14,363
Yes, Mother.

418
00:26:14,363 --> 00:26:16,165
Would you like some more pickled radish?
Okay, here's the coke.

419
00:26:16,499 --> 00:26:18,200
- More sauce?
- Yes.

420
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:19,268
Just a moment, please.

421
00:26:19,268 --> 00:26:22,538
- Here's a soda on the house.
- Enjoy, and please come again.

422
00:26:22,538 --> 00:26:25,641
<i>We'll put your donation</i>
<i>to the Merchants' Association to good use.</i>

423
00:26:25,641 --> 00:26:29,545
<i>It would be good to publicize this</i>
<i>to show our support for our tenants,</i>

424
00:26:29,545 --> 00:26:31,847
<i>but it's a shame</i>
<i>you wish to remain anonymous.</i>

425
00:26:31,847 --> 00:26:35,618
<i>Thank you for the chicken.</i>
<i>My kids are so excited.</i>

426
00:26:36,018 --> 00:26:37,219
<i>We will really enjoy it.</i>

427
00:26:37,253 --> 00:26:38,621
Thank you.

428
00:26:46,095 --> 00:26:48,030
- In the VIP lounge of the casino...
- Yes, what can I get for you?

429
00:26:48,030 --> 00:26:50,466
The sniper incident
that killed Chairman Cheon...

430
00:26:50,466 --> 00:26:52,201
is once again gaining public attention.

431
00:26:52,234 --> 00:26:55,638
Chairman Cheon, known as
Kingfisher's first civilian victim,

432
00:26:55,671 --> 00:26:57,440
was considered an entrepreneur
who contributed...

433
00:26:57,473 --> 00:26:59,275
greatly to the Gangwon region's economy...

434
00:26:59,775 --> 00:27:02,445
I knew something like this would happen.

435
00:27:02,478 --> 00:27:05,181
He was getting cocky,
calling himself a hero.

436
00:27:05,181 --> 00:27:08,717
If they killed an innocent person,
they deserve to be punished too.

437
00:27:08,751 --> 00:27:10,119
Kingfisher should be locked up.

438
00:27:10,186 --> 00:27:12,588
I'll get you the sauce.
Hey, one more order of sauce.

439
00:27:12,588 --> 00:27:13,823
- Sauce, got it.
- Okay.

440
00:27:13,823 --> 00:27:16,325
- When is the fried chicken coming out?
- The fried chicken? When is it ready?

441
00:27:16,358 --> 00:27:18,094
- It's ready now.
- It'll be right out.

442
00:27:18,127 --> 00:27:20,329
Along with the precise details
of Chairman Cheon's death,

443
00:27:20,362 --> 00:27:23,599
authorities are also expanding their
investigation into Kingfisher's motive.

444
00:27:23,599 --> 00:27:26,368
What do these people take Kingfisher for?

445
00:27:26,368 --> 00:27:27,503
What are we going to do?

446
00:27:27,503 --> 00:27:29,839
Manager Yu is going to be so upset
when she finds out.

447
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:31,006
She'll be devastated.

448
00:27:31,741 --> 00:27:33,309
For 16 years,

449
00:27:33,342 --> 00:27:36,112
it's the most important principle
she has strictly upheld.

450
00:27:36,145 --> 00:27:37,480
(Kingfisher:
First Innocent Civilian Victim?)

451
00:27:42,952 --> 00:27:44,153
Manager Yu sent a text.

452
00:27:44,787 --> 00:27:46,055
What does it say?

453
00:27:46,455 --> 00:27:47,790
(Trustworthy Police, Safe Nation)

454
00:27:47,790 --> 00:27:49,825
Hey, get rid of the reporters at the door.

455
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:53,129
Damn it. That bastard Kingfisher...

456
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:55,931
Why the hell did he come to this
backwater town to stir up trouble?

457
00:27:56,799 --> 00:27:58,100
What a mess.

458
00:28:00,736 --> 00:28:04,473
Gosh, what have you been digging for
all this time?

459
00:28:04,507 --> 00:28:06,809
You went to the scene, didn't you?

460
00:28:07,610 --> 00:28:09,412
Anyone could see that...

461
00:28:09,412 --> 00:28:12,047
their two heads just happened
to line up at that exact moment.

462
00:28:12,648 --> 00:28:14,683
Looks like Chairman Cheon
has a criminal record.

463
00:28:14,683 --> 00:28:18,988
You mean the rape case?
Oh, that was a long time ago.

464
00:28:19,021 --> 00:28:20,089
(Two Construction Workers Died)

465
00:28:20,089 --> 00:28:22,992
What about the two workers who died
at a construction site recently?

466
00:28:23,492 --> 00:28:25,928
That was ruled long ago
as an accidental fall and a suicide.

467
00:28:25,928 --> 00:28:27,797
Those cases were closed.

468
00:28:29,098 --> 00:28:31,300
I mean,
reporters came snooping around about that,

469
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:33,869
but there was nothing there,
so it never became a story.

470
00:28:36,739 --> 00:28:38,741
- Unbelievable.
- We have breaking news.

471
00:28:38,741 --> 00:28:39,809
The casino incident,

472
00:28:39,809 --> 00:28:42,445
which was thought to involve
Kingfisher's first civilian victim...

473
00:28:42,445 --> 00:28:43,512
Sir. Sir, look at that.

474
00:28:43,512 --> 00:28:45,381
- Chairman Cheon's...
- Turn it up.

475
00:28:45,414 --> 00:28:47,116
The full story has been revealed.

476
00:28:47,116 --> 00:28:49,118
According to one news report,
Chairman Cheon...

477
00:28:49,118 --> 00:28:51,387
hired the wife of one
of his construction workers...

478
00:28:51,387 --> 00:28:52,388
as a housekeeper...

479
00:28:52,421 --> 00:28:54,356
and then repeatedly
sexually assaulted her.

480
00:28:54,390 --> 00:28:55,925
- When her husband later found out...
- No way.

481
00:28:55,925 --> 00:28:59,995
and urged him to confess to the police,
Cheon bribed another worker...

482
00:28:59,995 --> 00:29:03,265
- to have the husband murdered.
- What... What is that?

483
00:29:03,299 --> 00:29:05,901
This was revealed
by the construction worker's wife herself.

484
00:29:05,935 --> 00:29:10,139
This should put to rest the controversy
that Kingfisher had claimed...

485
00:29:10,139 --> 00:29:11,707
their first innocent victim.

486
00:29:11,741 --> 00:29:15,711
Police are confirming the facts
of the report,

487
00:29:15,711 --> 00:29:17,947
and they are also looking into
additional criminal allegations...

488
00:29:17,947 --> 00:29:19,482
- against Chairman Cheon...
- Nice.

489
00:29:19,482 --> 00:29:21,784
Launched an internal investigation.
Online, Kingfisher is...

490
00:29:21,784 --> 00:29:24,854
Reporter Koo, congratulations.
A total scoop.

491
00:29:24,887 --> 00:29:26,622
Yes, thank you.

492
00:29:26,655 --> 00:29:27,757
(Investigative Reporting Team)

493
00:29:28,290 --> 00:29:29,291
Reporter Koo.

494
00:29:30,326 --> 00:29:33,028
