608
00:38:06,605 --> 00:38:07,640
Hm!

609
00:38:07,673 --> 00:38:10,409
- It's delicious.
- It is, right? Go on.

610
00:38:11,610 --> 00:38:14,280
Work must be really tough these days.

611
00:38:14,913 --> 00:38:17,249
Not at all. Your brother helps me out
so much. It's fine.

612
00:38:17,783 --> 00:38:18,817
And I have you to count on too.

613
00:38:18,851 --> 00:38:21,153
Oh, I haven't done anything.

614
00:38:22,921 --> 00:38:24,323
Se Ah, are you here for your allowance?

615
00:38:24,356 --> 00:38:25,357
Of course not.

616
00:38:25,858 --> 00:38:27,826
What about your coworkers?
Are they nice to you?

617
00:38:29,094 --> 00:38:32,164
They're so helpful.
I'm settling in without any problems.

618
00:38:32,831 --> 00:38:35,734
They must all be really nice people.

619
00:38:37,002 --> 00:38:40,172
Shouldn't you treat them to a meal
or something?

620
00:38:40,639 --> 00:38:45,110
- All of a sudden?
- Have you ever had a housewarming party?

621
00:38:46,845 --> 00:38:48,414
A housewarming party?

622
00:38:48,414 --> 00:38:51,317
You invite them over,
give them a tour of the house,

623
00:38:51,317 --> 00:38:53,118
and treat them to a meal,
that kind of thing.

624
00:38:53,152 --> 00:38:55,020
No, I've never thought about it.

625
00:38:59,291 --> 00:39:00,559
Don't you know it's just as important

626
00:39:00,559 --> 00:39:02,528
for a husband to support
his wife's career?

627
00:39:02,962 --> 00:39:05,798
Working moms have to walk on eggshells
at the office.

628
00:39:05,798 --> 00:39:09,468
If you take care of things like this,
her life at work will be easier.

629
00:39:12,171 --> 00:39:13,238
You have a point.

630
00:39:14,239 --> 00:39:16,508
You just returned to work
after three years,

631
00:39:16,508 --> 00:39:18,978
and they're the wonderful people
who are taking such good care of you.

632
00:39:19,011 --> 00:39:22,748
You should make them a nice, warm meal
to show your gratitude. Right?

633
00:39:22,781 --> 00:39:25,150
That's what makes life worth living.

634
00:39:26,118 --> 00:39:27,353
Just think of it as a work dinner.

635
00:39:28,220 --> 00:39:29,521
Mm-hmm.

636
00:39:29,521 --> 00:39:31,824
A work dinner?

637
00:39:33,225 --> 00:39:35,527
(Durumi Electronics)

638
00:39:35,561 --> 00:39:36,729
Manager Yu...

639
00:39:37,896 --> 00:39:41,100
Why would she invite us to her home?

640
00:39:42,635 --> 00:39:44,536
It's true she's never had anyone over.

641
00:39:46,772 --> 00:39:49,975
Don't you think it's some kind of tactic
to blend in?

642
00:39:49,975 --> 00:39:52,878
Our Manager Yu is not the type
to play games like that.

643
00:39:53,178 --> 00:39:54,780
