725
00:44:01,126 --> 00:44:02,728
Half the stuff in here
belongs to the baby.

726
00:44:02,728 --> 00:44:04,363
So I'm finally here.

727
00:44:04,997 --> 00:44:07,499
I was so curious what it was like inside.

728
00:44:08,567 --> 00:44:11,003
Mom! Aunt Se Ah looks like a princess.

729
00:44:15,841 --> 00:44:17,109
She does, doesn't she?

730
00:44:21,080 --> 00:44:23,048
This is my youngest sister.

731
00:44:23,048 --> 00:44:26,118
She was here to help out today, and...

732
00:44:26,885 --> 00:44:29,722
Your sister helps with
your housewarming party?

733
00:44:30,422 --> 00:44:32,725
She's so sweet.

734
00:44:33,492 --> 00:44:34,860
It's nice to meet you all.

735
00:44:35,494 --> 00:44:37,296
My name is Kwon Se Ah.

736
00:44:41,533 --> 00:44:42,601
Honey.

737
00:44:44,870 --> 00:44:46,005
Have you been drinking?

738
00:44:50,709 --> 00:44:52,578
This is an incredible feast.

739
00:44:52,611 --> 00:44:54,380
You didn't make all this yourself,
did you?

740
00:44:55,547 --> 00:44:58,884
So you're saying you really made
this entire feast by yourself?

741
00:44:58,917 --> 00:45:01,553
I suggested we order a few things,

742
00:45:01,553 --> 00:45:03,989
but she insisted on
making everything herself.

743
00:45:03,989 --> 00:45:05,824
I made it all.

744
00:45:06,292 --> 00:45:09,628
For a housewarming party,
personally preparing the food with care...

745
00:45:09,628 --> 00:45:11,196
is what makes it meaningful.

746
00:45:12,464 --> 00:45:15,834
This dish is a mix of glass noodles,
meat, and vegetables.

747
00:45:15,834 --> 00:45:19,004
A classic celebratory dish
with beautiful colors.

748
00:45:19,038 --> 00:45:22,474
A meat dish that truly makes you feel
like an honored guest.

749
00:45:23,309 --> 00:45:25,144
And these savory pancakes are easy to eat,

750
00:45:25,611 --> 00:45:28,047
but you can feel the effort
that went into them.

751
00:45:28,080 --> 00:45:29,081
I made them.

752
00:45:30,115 --> 00:45:34,920
Really, thank you for helping me adjust
after I came back to work.

753
00:45:34,920 --> 00:45:36,121
I'm so grateful to all of you.

754
00:45:38,958 --> 00:45:42,628
I wanted to personally make a warm meal
for you all.

755
00:45:44,330 --> 00:45:47,666
I've been wanting to find a chance
to say this...

756
00:45:48,467 --> 00:45:50,402
It's not much, but please enjoy.

757
00:45:50,436 --> 00:45:51,904
What do you mean?

758
00:45:52,838 --> 00:45:54,106
You've prepared so much.

759
00:45:55,007 --> 00:45:58,243
- I'm going to eat so much today.
- Eat up.

760
00:45:58,277 --> 00:45:59,845
Thank you for the meal.

761
00:45:59,845 --> 00:46:01,380
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

762
00:46:01,914 --> 00:46:02,948
Come on, everyone, eat.

763
00:46:04,149 --> 00:46:06,085
Please, enjoy.

764
00:46:11,457 --> 00:46:13,292
I heard from my sister-in-law
that you enjoy this from time to time,

765
00:46:13,292 --> 00:46:14,460
Assistant Manager Ki.

766
00:46:15,127 --> 00:46:19,098
So I prepared some for you.

767
00:46:20,599 --> 00:46:21,834
Please enjoy.

768
00:46:23,836 --> 00:46:25,237
Go ahead and eat.

769
00:46:25,771 --> 00:46:28,107
- Want some ribs? I'll cut them for you.
- Yes.

770
00:46:28,140 --> 00:46:30,676
Here, I'll do it. You eat.
You didn't even have lunch.

771
00:46:30,709 --> 00:46:33,212
You eat a lot.
Would you like some of that?

772
00:46:33,212 --> 00:46:35,648
Mmm! You two are so sweet.

773
00:46:37,049 --> 00:46:39,952
May I ask how you two first met?

774
00:46:42,254 --> 00:46:43,989
We...

775
00:46:44,023 --> 00:46:47,793
We just met here and there.

776
00:46:47,793 --> 00:46:50,329
Actually, a pickpocket
brought us together.

777
00:46:50,362 --> 00:46:51,597
A pickpocket?

778
00:46:51,597 --> 00:46:54,633
Yes. About eight years ago,
I was covering a pickpocketing story,

779
00:46:54,633 --> 00:46:56,168
and I ended up with a serious head injury.

780
00:46:56,235 --> 00:47:00,139
Oh my, so you were
in a terrible situation.

781
00:47:00,139 --> 00:47:04,209
But luckily, a woman called 911 for me,

782
00:47:04,243 --> 00:47:05,577
and I barely made it out alive.

783
00:47:06,545 --> 00:47:08,847
The hospital told me that
if I'd arrived any later,

784
00:47:08,847 --> 00:47:09,982
I might not have made it.

785
00:47:11,684 --> 00:47:13,819
So after I woke up
about four months later...

786
00:47:13,819 --> 00:47:16,622
The first time I could walk,
I went up to the hospital rooftop,

787
00:47:16,655 --> 00:47:19,291
and that's when I met Bo Na.

788
00:47:19,692 --> 00:47:23,028
<i>That day, I saw Bo Na's bright smile,</i>

789
00:47:23,062 --> 00:47:25,464
and I fell in love at first sight.

790
00:47:26,765 --> 00:47:29,234
How romantic!

791
00:47:29,234 --> 00:47:32,705
So you two have a love story like that.

792
00:47:33,872 --> 00:47:35,574
That's so moving.
To think you were brought together

793
00:47:35,608 --> 00:47:38,644
- on the verge of life and death.
- It is.

794
00:47:39,111 --> 00:47:42,314
By any chance,
the woman who called 911 back then...

795
00:47:42,748 --> 00:47:43,749
Do you know who she was?

796
00:47:44,883 --> 00:47:47,486
I actually looked into it
with the 911 dispatch center...

797
00:47:47,486 --> 00:47:48,721
as soon as I woke up,

798
00:47:48,721 --> 00:47:52,157
but the call was made from my phone,
so they couldn't get her contact info.

799
00:47:52,157 --> 00:47:55,761
And they only remembered
that the caller was a woman.

800
00:47:56,495 --> 00:47:59,598
Well, I'm sure she'll be
greatly rewarded for that.

801
00:48:00,332 --> 00:48:02,835
She's the one who saved your life. Right?

802
00:48:03,235 --> 00:48:06,305
Then isn't the woman
the one who brought you together,

803
00:48:06,305 --> 00:48:08,040
not the pickpocket?

804
00:48:10,609 --> 00:48:11,744
Now that you mention it, you're right.

805
00:48:12,311 --> 00:48:14,647
I should find her somehow
and thank her, right?

806
00:48:14,647 --> 00:48:15,648
Oh, you should.

807
00:48:16,148 --> 00:48:17,883
- You just have to find her.
- Yes, I will.

808
00:48:17,883 --> 00:48:20,085
- Come on, dig in.
- It's getting cold. Please, eat up.

809
00:48:21,687 --> 00:48:23,656
Here, Assistant Manager Ki.

810
00:48:25,024 --> 00:48:28,127
You should have some meat too,
Assistant Manager Ki. Here.

811
00:48:29,828 --> 00:48:32,331
Oh no. Just a second. This...

812
00:48:33,098 --> 00:48:35,000
- Oh no.
- Oh, what do I do? This wet wipe...

813
00:48:35,501 --> 00:48:37,303
I'm so sorry, Assistant Manager Ki.

814
00:48:37,336 --> 00:48:38,637
I'm all right.

815
00:48:39,071 --> 00:48:40,372
Do you have any cold beer?

816
00:48:40,706 --> 00:48:43,642
Beer? I'll get some for you right away.

817
00:48:45,778 --> 00:48:48,714
Here, I'll open it for you.

818
00:49:01,727 --> 00:49:02,728
Oh no.

819
00:49:09,668 --> 00:49:10,669
At least take this...

820
00:49:21,614 --> 00:49:23,148
(8 Years Ago, Spring)

821
00:49:23,716 --> 00:49:26,118
I've never applied to this company.

822
00:49:26,685 --> 00:49:27,920
There must be some kind of mistake...

823
00:49:27,920 --> 00:49:31,991
You must have been surprised to have
an application sent by email so suddenly.

824
00:49:32,925 --> 00:49:35,628
You were kidnapped as a child.

825
00:49:35,628 --> 00:49:38,631
Your major is psychology,
but your specialty is hacking.

826
00:49:42,067 --> 00:49:43,669
Durumi Electronics Sales Team Three.

827
00:49:45,337 --> 00:49:47,439
I think you do things differently
from the other departments.

828
00:49:55,414 --> 00:49:56,649
Please continue.

829
00:49:56,649 --> 00:49:58,450
Even your transaction performance chart...

830
00:49:58,450 --> 00:50:00,753
looks subtly different
from other departments,

831
00:50:00,753 --> 00:50:03,689
as if you pieced it together
by splicing real data.

832
00:50:04,123 --> 00:50:06,558
The same goes for the ratio
of off-site work in your logs.

833
00:50:06,558 --> 00:50:10,162
So, did you figure out what they do?

834
00:50:11,030 --> 00:50:14,199
Only that it's illegal.

835
00:50:16,101 --> 00:50:17,102
That's right.

836
00:50:18,037 --> 00:50:21,974
Sales Team Three carefully selects
and eliminates criminals.

837
00:50:24,543 --> 00:50:26,612
For various reasons,
I'm pleased with your qualifications,

838
00:50:26,612 --> 00:50:27,746
Mr. Ki Young Do.

839
00:50:28,480 --> 00:50:30,516
What happens if I refuse?

840
00:50:33,752 --> 00:50:36,388
We only make offers to people
who won't refuse.

841
00:50:38,090 --> 00:50:41,260
Still, if I refuse, will you kill me?

842
00:50:47,666 --> 00:50:49,134
You need to keep it a secret.

843
00:50:58,510 --> 00:51:01,347
What will you do? Will you keep my secret?

844
00:51:06,986 --> 00:51:08,087
Don't be such a chicken.

845
00:51:23,335 --> 00:51:24,870
Eat this and relax, rookie.

846
00:51:33,946 --> 00:51:36,315
This is the best thing for stress. Eat up.

847
00:52:00,973 --> 00:52:01,974
I'm so screwed.

848
00:52:03,142 --> 00:52:04,810
I'm so screwed.

849
00:52:06,111 --> 00:52:08,213
Oh, I should just leave this house.

850
00:52:09,081 --> 00:52:10,249
I should just go die.

851
00:52:13,452 --> 00:52:14,486
Oh dear.

852
00:52:15,779 --> 00:52:16,881
Let's have some fruit.

853
00:52:16,914 --> 00:52:18,749
Yul, come here.

854
00:52:19,149 --> 00:52:21,719
Oh, Yul, want some strawberries?

855
00:52:23,254 --> 00:52:25,289
Okay, let's toast. Cheers.

856
00:52:25,322 --> 00:52:27,958
I'm sorry for causing trouble.

857
00:52:28,526 --> 00:52:30,694
I'll be heading out first.

858
00:52:30,694 --> 00:52:31,729
- Where do you think you're going?
- This is perfect.

859
00:52:31,729 --> 00:52:33,264
Since Assistant Manager Ki is leaving,

860
00:52:33,297 --> 00:52:34,999
so you should walk him to the main road.

861
00:52:34,999 --> 00:52:36,467
He's taking the subway,
so go to the back gate.

862
00:52:36,967 --> 00:52:38,369
- Me?
- Yes.

863
00:52:39,036 --> 00:52:41,272
- Why?
- What? He doesn't know the way.

864
00:52:42,306 --> 00:52:45,209
Oh, right. Assistant Manager Ki,
go on ahead.

865
00:52:45,209 --> 00:52:46,844
- We'll leave in a little bit.
- Go on.

866
00:52:46,844 --> 00:52:48,245
All right, everyone.

867
00:52:48,245 --> 00:52:50,047
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

868
00:52:52,182 --> 00:52:53,551
Assistant Manager Ki.

869
00:52:53,984 --> 00:52:57,154
I'll be sure to wash your clothes
and return them.

870
00:52:57,655 --> 00:52:58,656
Fine.

871
00:53:00,524 --> 00:53:02,293
Are you very upset?

872
00:53:03,027 --> 00:53:04,161
I'm not thrilled.

873
00:53:04,929 --> 00:53:07,131
Oh, so you're not thrilled.

874
00:53:07,131 --> 00:53:08,599
This is all because of me...

875
00:53:21,612 --> 00:53:22,980
Can't your brother lift a finger?

876
00:53:24,548 --> 00:53:25,549
Lift a finger?

877
00:53:30,788 --> 00:53:31,789
Lift a finger?

878
00:53:39,597 --> 00:53:41,265
When are you going to return my clothes?

879
00:53:43,334 --> 00:53:45,870
Soon? Yes.

880
00:53:47,371 --> 00:53:48,472
The day you return the clothes,

881
00:53:49,573 --> 00:53:50,608
let's go on a date.

882
00:54:07,224 --> 00:54:09,727
A date?

883
00:54:13,664 --> 00:54:14,732
That was a great meal.

884
00:54:14,732 --> 00:54:16,534
I ate so well. I'm so full.

885
00:54:18,502 --> 00:54:20,871
Oh, by the way, we did a good job, right?

886
00:54:21,605 --> 00:54:22,973
Yes, I think we did well.

887
00:54:25,543 --> 00:54:26,710
We didn't make any mistakes, did we?

888
00:54:28,345 --> 00:54:31,348
- I don't think we made any mistakes.
- Right. Good.

889
00:54:33,250 --> 00:54:37,221
Honestly, Manager Yu's cooking
is just so-so, right?

890
00:54:39,256 --> 00:54:40,991
Oh, my goodness.

891
00:54:42,860 --> 00:54:46,363
Do you think we won't need to erase
that CCTV record?

892
00:54:46,363 --> 00:54:47,531
Oh, Team Leader.

893
00:54:47,531 --> 00:54:49,867
We didn't come here for a Meeting today.

894
00:54:49,900 --> 00:54:52,369
Right. Hey, let's just act normal.

895
00:54:52,403 --> 00:54:54,305
Act normal, okay?

896
00:55:00,077 --> 00:55:01,712
Get in.

897
00:55:01,712 --> 00:55:04,048
- Let's go.
- Thank you.

898
00:55:09,620 --> 00:55:10,621
Excuse me.

899
00:55:12,623 --> 00:55:14,258
I think you might have dropped this.

900
00:55:17,628 --> 00:55:18,629
Thank you.

901
00:55:20,497 --> 00:55:21,498
Thank you.

902
00:55:31,008 --> 00:55:32,109
Let's go.

903
00:55:37,948 --> 00:55:39,917
- Uncle.
- Gosh, my little princess.

904
00:55:39,917 --> 00:55:42,253
- Hey.
- Wow, my little princess.

905
00:55:43,587 --> 00:55:46,724
Uncle, did you catch a lot of bad guys?

906
00:55:47,291 --> 00:55:48,893
I caught this many.

907
00:55:49,493 --> 00:55:50,961
Okay, Yul. Come on.

908
00:55:51,428 --> 00:55:52,429
All right, attention.

909
00:55:53,330 --> 00:55:56,467
This uncle protects good kids like Yul.
I'm a...

910
00:55:56,867 --> 00:55:59,436
- Policeman.
- That's right. Good job.

911
00:56:00,337 --> 00:56:02,840
- Let's go.
- You're early, guess you're not busy.

912
00:56:02,840 --> 00:56:04,375
Hey, Bo Na said she's making
braised short ribs.

913
00:56:04,375 --> 00:56:07,111
What could be more important than that?
Now, go play.

914
00:56:07,111 --> 00:56:08,646
Dong Jin, you're here.

915
00:56:09,547 --> 00:56:11,448
Thank you for having me over again.

916
00:56:11,482 --> 00:56:13,284
Oh, it was nothing.

917
00:56:13,284 --> 00:56:15,819
Why does she always insist on inviting you
whenever she cooks?

918
00:56:16,287 --> 00:56:18,455
- It's a bad habit.
- Why?

919
00:56:18,455 --> 00:56:20,758
It means that
while I'm unlucky in friends,

920
00:56:20,758 --> 00:56:22,126
I'm very lucky
when it comes to their wives.

921
00:56:23,160 --> 00:56:24,695
You should worry about
finding your own wife.

922
00:56:26,197 --> 00:56:27,698
You should come by more often.

923
00:56:27,698 --> 00:56:30,000
Yul gets really excited
when she hears you're coming over, Uncle.

924
00:56:30,768 --> 00:56:32,803
You got it. I'll do that.

925
00:56:32,836 --> 00:56:35,439
Anyway, it must be tough for you
now that you're back at work.

926
00:56:35,439 --> 00:56:38,175
You should make this guy help you more.
He's always been so coddled,

927
00:56:38,175 --> 00:56:39,643
so I doubt there's much
he knows how to do.

928
00:56:39,643 --> 00:56:41,345
I'm actually good at everything now.
All right?

929
00:56:42,179 --> 00:56:44,215
Honey, what else should I do?
Just say the word.

930
00:56:44,748 --> 00:56:47,284
His heart's in the right place.
He's just not very talented...

931
00:56:47,284 --> 00:56:49,820
Just a moment. I'll go get you something.

932
00:56:50,354 --> 00:56:52,389
Thank you. I'm in your debt.

933
00:56:53,123 --> 00:56:55,025
- Sit down.
- No, it's all right.

934
00:56:56,060 --> 00:56:57,828
Looks like you had company?

935
00:56:57,828 --> 00:56:59,530
Yeah, my wife's coworkers.

936
00:56:59,530 --> 00:57:01,732
Oh, that must've been them
leaving just now.

937
00:57:01,765 --> 00:57:04,501
- You saw them?
- Yes, by the first-floor elevator.

938
00:57:04,902 --> 00:57:06,503
They seemed really nice.

939
00:57:11,275 --> 00:57:13,110
I'll have home-cooked meals for a week.

940
00:57:13,110 --> 00:57:14,778
Seriously, Bo Na... Every time...

941
00:57:15,246 --> 00:57:16,580
I helped with that.

942
00:57:17,414 --> 00:57:20,017
- You should thank me.
- For which part?

943
00:57:20,017 --> 00:57:21,185
Tell me so I can throw it out right now.

944
00:57:21,185 --> 00:57:22,186
Will you?

945
00:57:22,186 --> 00:57:24,722
You said you'd repay us, right? With what?

946
00:57:25,389 --> 00:57:27,925
Do I have money?
Do I have connections?

947
00:57:27,925 --> 00:57:31,228
Wow, you're already going back
on your word.

948
00:57:31,228 --> 00:57:34,064
As a cop, the only thing I know how to do
is protect people.

949
00:57:36,467 --> 00:57:37,935
Except for you, you jerk.

950
00:57:37,935 --> 00:57:40,471
I'm only going to protect
sweet Bo Na and lovely Yul.

951
00:57:41,672 --> 00:57:43,707
I can protect my own wife and daughter.

952
00:57:48,145 --> 00:57:51,815
Make sure you treat her extra well
on birthdays and holidays.

953
00:57:52,983 --> 00:57:54,285
Not having a family...

954
00:57:55,986 --> 00:57:58,222
is a very lonely and painful thing.

955
00:58:34,491 --> 00:58:37,127
So what was it you wanted to know?

956
00:58:37,595 --> 00:58:39,697
You didn't write that
Cheon Seong Gil article.

957
00:58:40,331 --> 00:58:41,799
I co-wrote it with a junior reporter.

958
00:58:44,001 --> 00:58:45,336
If you don't want to talk about it,
forget it.

959
00:58:45,836 --> 00:58:48,939
Well, anyway, thanks to that article,
Kingfisher's reputation was saved.

960
00:58:53,043 --> 00:58:55,145
Is Kingfisher still giving you
the runaround?

961
00:58:57,414 --> 00:59:00,284
They came back with a vengeance.

962
00:59:01,819 --> 00:59:03,754
They've never operated on
such a tight schedule before.

963
00:59:04,989 --> 00:59:06,624
If they take another break like this,

964
00:59:07,024 --> 00:59:09,360
they'll be on track to wipe out
every criminal in the world.

965
00:59:09,994 --> 00:59:10,995
This is the second one.

966
00:59:11,862 --> 00:59:13,097
- What is?
- The hiatus.

967
00:59:13,097 --> 00:59:14,865
There was one eight years ago.

968
00:59:14,865 --> 00:59:17,167
Around the time of the World Cup,
after that incident.

969
00:59:19,069 --> 00:59:20,170
Was it for nine months?

970
00:59:20,204 --> 00:59:22,306
When they came back that time,
everyone was curious too.

971
00:59:22,740 --> 00:59:24,141
Wondering what could have happened
during that time...

972
00:59:24,875 --> 00:59:27,077
You know what happened to me
during that time, right?

973
00:59:28,245 --> 00:59:29,747
I met Yu Bo Na.

974
00:59:31,248 --> 00:59:34,351
Did you save Kwon Tae Sung that day?

975
00:59:34,818 --> 00:59:35,819
Yes.

976
00:59:36,220 --> 00:59:37,588
Why?

977
00:59:37,588 --> 00:59:38,589
Because I wanted to.

978
00:59:39,089 --> 00:59:40,558
It could have been dangerous.

979
00:59:41,559 --> 00:59:43,527
It could have been, but luckily it wasn't.

980
00:59:44,962 --> 00:59:47,031
You were secretly happy back then.

981
00:59:47,064 --> 00:59:49,633
When Kingfisher returned
after the first hiatus.

982
00:59:50,401 --> 00:59:51,735
I thought you'd be happy this time too.

983
00:59:52,203 --> 00:59:54,538
You used to be so desperate
to meet Kingfisher.

984
00:59:54,538 --> 00:59:56,440
What, have you lost interest now?

985
00:59:57,841 --> 00:59:58,943
I can't meet them.

986
00:59:59,577 --> 01:00:02,279
<i> What happened after that?</i>

987
01:00:03,547 --> 01:00:05,816
He saved me.

988
01:00:07,251 --> 01:00:08,519
And I came back.

989
01:00:09,453 --> 01:00:10,521
Then...

990
01:00:11,021 --> 01:00:12,122
That's right. It was my husband.

991
01:00:13,490 --> 01:00:15,459
He's the one who made me come back.

992
01:00:16,160 --> 01:00:17,728
<i>They shouldn't have come back.</i>

993
01:00:19,096 --> 01:00:20,197
This time.

994
01:00:20,197 --> 01:00:22,933
He also made me return as Kingfisher.

995
01:00:23,634 --> 01:00:24,735
They should have stayed away.

996
01:00:25,669 --> 01:00:28,472
It was Kwon Tae Sung. That's him.

997
01:00:29,773 --> 01:00:33,844
(December 2018)

998
01:00:33,844 --> 01:00:36,013
It's cold now, so when it gets warmer...

999
01:00:36,447 --> 01:00:38,215
How about we talk about it then?

1000
01:00:39,884 --> 01:00:41,852
I made this decision
after thinking about it for a long time.

1001
01:00:42,253 --> 01:00:43,254
I know.

1002
01:00:43,888 --> 01:00:45,122
But you never know.

1003
01:00:45,756 --> 01:00:46,924
Maybe you'll change your mind...

1004
01:00:46,924 --> 01:00:48,025
when flowers bloom,
and the spring wind blows.

1005
01:00:52,263 --> 01:00:54,265
I don't want to do anything anymore.

1006
01:00:59,236 --> 01:01:00,404
Take a vacation, starting today.

1007
01:01:00,437 --> 01:01:02,540
Take as much time off as you need.

1008
01:01:03,007 --> 01:01:06,010
Yes, you should take a trip.
What do you say?

1009
01:01:07,044 --> 01:01:09,780
Does anyone have a travel recommendation
for Yu Bo Na?

1010
01:01:10,514 --> 01:01:12,349
Somewhere with nice mountains
and fresh air.

1011
01:01:12,349 --> 01:01:13,684
A place where
she doesn't have to do a thing.

1012
01:01:14,852 --> 01:01:16,887
Well, that would be...

1013
01:01:22,326 --> 01:01:23,561
How about here?

1014
01:01:23,928 --> 01:01:26,397
It's quiet, there's no one around,
and your phone won't work.

1015
01:01:27,598 --> 01:01:29,466
And I hear they serve three meals a day.

1016
01:01:32,770 --> 01:01:36,740
Right, for a trip, you need the ocean.
It really clears your head, you know?

1017
01:01:36,774 --> 01:01:39,109
Right, you can take
a boat ride too. It's perfect.

1018
01:01:39,777 --> 01:01:40,811
You should go there.

1019
01:01:40,811 --> 01:01:43,414
If you still feel the same when back,

1020
01:01:44,181 --> 01:01:45,616
I'll accept your resignation.

1021
01:01:46,383 --> 01:01:47,618
Okay?

1022
01:01:49,520 --> 01:01:50,955
(Unrim Mountain Lodge)

1023
01:02:14,945 --> 01:02:17,047
I wonder why she's acting like that.
She's not even eating.

1024
01:02:17,615 --> 01:02:19,049
She skipped another meal.

1025
01:02:19,516 --> 01:02:21,485
I'm really worried.

1026
01:04:50,467 --> 01:04:54,605
(A Bona Fide Killer)

1027
01:04:54,638 --> 01:04:57,074
Bo Na, what do you think of
when you see icicles?

1028
01:04:57,074 --> 01:04:58,976
That they'd be perfect for hitting
a vital point in one go.

1029
01:04:59,410 --> 01:05:02,346
<i>I've never really found</i>
<i>anything to be pretty.</i>

1030
01:05:02,379 --> 01:05:04,014
<i>I'll show you</i>
<i>plenty of them from now on.</i>

1031
01:05:04,014 --> 01:05:05,649
<i>They say all the roads up the mountain</i>
<i>have been closed...</i>

1032
01:05:05,649 --> 01:05:07,051
<i>since yesterday afternoon.</i>

1033
01:05:07,051 --> 01:05:08,452
<i>I think we're stranded.</i>

1034
01:05:10,154 --> 01:05:11,655
Bo Na.

1035
01:05:11,689 --> 01:05:13,224
Why did you do it right after
you got out of prison?

1036
01:05:13,290 --> 01:05:15,526
This is all because you cops
can't catch Kingfisher.

1037
01:05:15,526 --> 01:05:19,029
To me, Kingfisher is nothing
but a psychopathic murderer.

1038
01:05:19,063 --> 01:05:21,198
You're the family of one of the victims.

1039
01:05:21,198 --> 01:05:22,833
Can I borrow this for the weekend?

1040
01:05:22,833 --> 01:05:26,537
I have a confession to make.
I know who Kingfisher is.

1041
01:05:30,641 --> 01:05:32,643
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
